\procedure dollars-stay-literal(a:"one", b:"two")
A \PROCEDURE BODY SUBSTITUTES NOTHING. Only a `\define` body performs `$param$`/`$(var)$`/`${filter}$`
substitution — widget.js gates both placeholder forms behind `isMacroDefinition` — so the three
placeholders below stand as ordinary text.
$a$ and $(b)$ and ${ [all[current]] }$
\end

\define dollars-substitute-here(a:"one", b:"two")
A \DEFINE BODY SUBSTITUTES ALL THREE FORMS IN PLACE, so the parameter, the variable and the filter
each colour below exactly where the procedure above left plain text.
$a$ and $(b)$ and ${ [all[current]] }$
\end

