\procedure param-name-takes-an-open-paren(paren()
A PARAMETER NAME ADMITS AN OPEN PAREN. The host's name pattern excludes `:`, `)`, a comma and
whitespace, and nothing else — so it binds `paren(` as ONE name. The grammar reads that inner paren
as a separator instead, which costs a colour on a name no author writes and keeps the surrounding
reading intact.
\end

