[tag[Task]] :sort[title]
\end

\parameters(a:one,b:"two")

\parameters ($a:"one")

A PRAGMA READS ONLY AT THE TOP OF A TIDDLER. `wikiparser.js` runs `parsePragmas()` once, before
`parseBlocks()`, and never returns to it, so a `\procedure` line standing below body content — as
this one does, after the paragraphs and pragmas above — defines nothing and stands as body text,
whether or not its keyword carries the space its name demands. `pragmas.no-space.tw` isolates that
OTHER reason (a glued keyword and name) at a position where a spaced pragma still would define:

\procedure stands-below-body()

Body text after every definition above.

A substituted attribute value takes the same placeholders a define body takes, and takes them
outside any definition, so it stands here below the pragmas.

<$text text=`a variable $(currentTiddler)$ and a filter ${ [tag[Task]] }$ in a substituted attribute`/>

